            {
                "box": {
                    "id": "obj-56",
                    "linecount": 15,
                    "maxclass": "comment",
                    "numinlets": 1,
                    "numoutlets": 0,
                    "patching_rect": [ 1576.00004696846, 717.3333547115326, 368.66667544841766, 237.0 ],
                    "text": "This value represents \"tonality confidence\" (0.0 – 1.0).\n\nIt does NOT say what the sound *is*.\nIt says how strongly the signal behaves like a stable tone over time.\n\n0.0  = clearly noise / percussive / unstable\n0.5  = hybrid (noise + tone)\n1.0  = stable, sustained tone (safe to treat as tonal)\n\nThe value rises slowly when a pitch stays stable\nand falls when the signal becomes noisy or transient.\n\nAveraging this value over a short window (e.g. 50–100 ms)\ngives a reliable measure of whether that event was mostly\nnoise or mostly tonal.\n"
                }
            },
